# Pluto notebooks (Styx)

Cursor users are not always in Pluto. **Only bootstrap a Pluto session when the user requests notebook work.**

**Skills:**
- **pluto-session** — start Pluto, choose/open notebook, open Glass (user says "work on notebooks")
- **pluto-workflow** — cell edits once a notebook is open
- **pluto-semantics** — cell grammar and `pluto_multi_expression` fixes

Never ask the user to run `pluto-serve.sh` or `PlutoMCP.serve()` manually — use lifecycle MCP tools (`start_pluto_session`, `open_notebook`).

## Safe preview

Path B (`open_notebook` default) = **Safe preview**. **Remind** the user that edits won't execute and outputs won't update until they click **Run notebook code** in Glass — still edit when asked. If they ask you to run the notebook, point them to that button (not `run_all_cells`). See **pluto-workflow** skill.

## Cell edits (notebook already open)

1. Design Mode (**Cmd+Shift+D**) click → **`resolve_pluto_context`** → **`read_cell`** (remind about safe preview if active)
2. Stage → **`submit_changes`** once → re-read for errors

## Safety

Re-read before overwriting browser drafts. **`submit_changes`** before ending turn if staged.
